  "executive_scientific_conclusion": "Standard ANOVA p-values (p < 0.0001 for returns, p < 1e-15 for MAE) are severely inflated by the moving-average overlap of consecutive hourly bars. For a 24h horizon, 95.83% of the window is shared between adjacent bars, reducing the effective sample size from 18,767 bars down to 781 blocks. Under non-overlapping subsampling and stationary block bootstrap, forward risk separation (MAE) remains robustly significant due to strong volatility persistence, but forward return predictability is categorized as 'STATISTICAL_SIGNIFICANCE_NOT_ESTABLISHED' or at most 'EXPLORATORY_PREDICTIVE_EVIDENCE'. All overstatements of mathematical certainty have been systematically corrected."
